{"resource": {"name": "Bacteria Sample Data", "id": "e49x-tw9b", "resource_name": null, "parent_fxf": [], "description": "Samples are taken daily at locations throughout the distribution system. Temperature, pH, and Total Chlorine Residual are collected by city personnel. Samples are taken to a lab to be analyzed for Total Coliform and E. Coli indicators. Results are returned to the city the following business day.", "attribution": null, "attribution_link": null, "contact_email": null, "type": "dataset", "updatedAt": "2024-09-17T10:35:06.000Z", "createdAt": "2018-10-31T19:18:11.000Z", "metadata_updated_at": "2024-09-17T10:35:02.000Z", "data_updated_at": "2024-09-17T10:35:06.000Z", "columns_name": ["DATE", "Number of Samples Taken", "Free Chlorine", "Street", "Replacement Address/Notes", "Total Chlorine Residual", "RESULTS", "Sample Type", "SITE #"], "columns_field_name": ["date", "number_of_samples_taken", "free_chlorine", "street", "replacement_address_or_notes", "total_chlorine_residual", "results", "replacement_sample", "site"], "columns_datatype": ["Calendar date", "Number", "Number", "Text", "Text", "Number", "Text", "Text", "Text"], "columns_description": ["Date test was conducted.", "Number of samples taken at the location.", "The amount of free chlorine as measured in mg/L. This number increases in Feb/Mar during the chlorine maintenance period. Instruments have an accuracy of plus or minus 0.1 mg/L.", "Street name for where water sample was collected.", "Indicates the location of replacement samples, special samples, or any notes associated with the sample.", "The level of chlorine disinfectant by measuring chloramines (minimum requirement is .5 mg/L). Instruments have an accuracy of plus or minus 0.1 mg/L.", "Provides results from the laboratory to indicate pass, fail, or if sample was rejected.", "Bacteria Samples are routine and collected every 30 days. If a sample has an error, is rejected, or has bacteria present, a replacement sample is taken. This co